<title>SWEDEN: FORECASTS-Nordbanken's Swedish economic forecasts.</title>
<headline>FORECASTS-Nordbanken's Swedish economic forecasts.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-04-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sweden's state-controlled bank Nordbanken on Thursday released the following forecasts for the Swedish economy.</p>
<p>					1997    1998    1999*   2000*</p>
<p> CPI (yr average)		  0.5     2.1     2.4    2.9</p>
<p> Hourly wages			4.5     3.8     3,7    4.0</p>
<p> Unemployment			8.4     7.4     6.5    5.5</p>
<p> State's borrow need (Bln SKR) 0.0    -5.0   -12.0  -23.0</p>
<p> Industrial production	   3.5     5.0     5,3    4.8</p>
<p> Current account (pct of GDP)  3.1     3.6     3.5    3.5</p>
<p> Trade balance (Bln SKR)     129.0   144.0   140.0  141.0</p>
<p> Gross Domestic Product	   1.7    3.5     3.8    3.3</p>
<p> Private consumption		1.6    2.8     3.6    2.9</p>
<p> Public consumption		 0.0   -0.1    -0.1    0.2</p>
<p> Exports				5.7    7.4     7.0    5.4</p>
<p> Imports				3.9    6.8     7.8    6.6</p>
<p> Repo rate			   4.10    5.0     6.25   6.25</p>
<p> Ten year bond yield (pct)     7.0     7.25    7.5    6.75</p>
<p> SEK/DEM			     4.40    4.40</p>
<p> SEK/USD			     7.70    7.48</p>
<p> DEM/USD			     1.75    1.70</p>
<p>*) Years 1999 and 2000 are outlooks, not forecasts</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1017</p>
</text>
